# Cloudflare Pages response headers — the cache contract, in the repo.
#
# Ports the nine Cache Rules + one Transform Rule documented in
# docs/architecture/architecture-deploy.md §"Cache strategy" out of dashboard UI
# state that no test covers, no diff shows, and no clone reproduces. §Phase 4 of
# docs/plans/20260830-plan-cloudflare-pages-deploy.md.
#
# HOW PAGES READS THIS FILE, measured rather than assumed: every matching rule
# applies and their headers are COMBINED, not overridden. A catch-all plus a
# specific rule therefore yields
#     cache-control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=300, public, max-age=31536000
# and a browser takes the FIRST max-age — so the specific rule loses, silently and
# backwards. The documented way to override a more pervasive rule is to detach the
# header first with `! Header-Name`, which every block below does. Verified on
# bh-blog.pages.dev; the first version of this file shipped the doubled header.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT YET AUTHORITATIVE ON THE LIVE SITE. The zone's Cache Rules are
# configured as "Ignore cache-control header and use this TTL", which overrides
# whatever the origin sends — including this. Until those rules are removed in the
# dashboard, `_headers` governs only the `.pages.dev` origin, where no Cache Rules
# apply. That ordering is deliberate: headers in, rules out, then drop the purge
# step, verifying at each stage.

# ── Class B: stable URL, changes every deploy ────────────────────────────────
# HTML, feeds, the JSON indexes, the agent-readable `.qmd` sources. Bookmarkable
# and SEO-indexed, so they cannot be fingerprinted. `max-age=0` makes browsers
# revalidate — this is what the pending `class-b-html-browser-revalidate`
# Transform Rule was for, and it stops being a pending dashboard action here.
# `s-maxage=300` bounds edge staleness at five minutes.
#
# The catch-all is Class B on purpose: a new file type nobody thought about lands
# on the conservative setting rather than being cached for a year.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=300

# ── Class C: stable URL, rarely changes ──────────────────────────────────────
# Post images are immutable in practice once published, but their URLs are not
# fingerprinted, so a day is the compromise the cache strategy already chose.
/posts/*.jpg
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/posts/*.jpeg
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/posts/*.png
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/posts/*.webp
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/posts/*.svg
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/favicon.svg
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/favicon-16x16.png
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/favicon-32x32.png
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/apple-touch-icon.png
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/og-default.png
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/robots.txt
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/.well-known/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# ── Class A: fingerprinted, safe to cache for a year ─────────────────────────
# The URL encodes a content hash, so changed content always gets a new URL.
# `cache-bust-css.py` produces `styles.<10-char-sha256>.css`.
/styles.*.css
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# DELIBERATE DEVIATION from the dashboard rules, which give all of `site_libs/**`
# a one-year immutable TTL. Only *some* of that tree is fingerprinted: Quarto
# hashes `bootstrap-<hash>.min.css` and `quarto-syntax-highlighting-<hash>.css`,
# but ships `quarto-nav.js`, `quarto-html/*.js` and the MathJax font files under
# stable names. A year of `immutable` on a stable-named file means a Quarto
# upgrade cannot reach browsers that already cached it — the existing rule is
# riskier than it looks, and `_headers` has no way to say "only the hashed ones".
# One day keeps the hit rate high and bounds the exposure; revisit if the asset
# volume ever justifies splitting the tree at build time.
/site_libs/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
